WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.648
OSINT draws from many public source categories, each with different strengths and limitations.

00:00:06.648 --> 00:00:14.672
Search engines help discover material, but their results are ranked, incomplete, personalized, and subject to change.

00:00:14.672 --> 00:00:21.320
Analysts should treat search results as discovery aids rather than evidence by themselves.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:28.885
Websites and official public records can provide direct statements, filings, policies, notices, and historical context.

00:00:28.885 --> 00:00:34.617
News organizations and specialist publications may add reporting and expert interpretation.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:43.557
Forums and social platforms can surface early observations, but identity, authenticity, motive, and context often require careful validation.

00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:51.581
Domain and DNS data can help describe public-facing infrastructure and relationships at a point in time.

00:00:51.581 --> 00:00:57.771
Code repositories may expose public project history, dependencies, documentation, or security advisories.

00:00:57.771 --> 00:01:07.629
Collection must remain within lawful public access and organizational policy; public-source work never authorizes access to private repositories or accounts.

00:01:07.629 --> 00:01:15.194
Images and video may contain visible objects, text, landmarks, weather, shadows, edits, or publication metadata.

00:01:15.194 --> 00:01:20.008
Maps and geospatial sources can help test location claims.

00:01:20.008 --> 00:01:28.490
Visual analysis should avoid identifying or tracking private individuals without lawful authority and a legitimate, proportionate purpose.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:31.929
Source selection should follow the requirement.

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:41.787
Official records may be strong for a legal filing, while direct technical documentation may be better for a software behavior.

00:01:41.787 --> 00:01:49.352
A social post may provide a lead but not enough support for a consequential judgment.

00:01:49.352 --> 00:01:57.376
Maintain a source inventory that records ownership, access conditions, update patterns, expected reliability, and preservation needs.

00:01:57.376 --> 00:02:06.316
Diversity matters: independent sources with different origins provide stronger corroboration than many sites repeating the same original claim.
